    <p class="tag">Specialised Service</p>
    <h1>Facing Criminal or Immigration Proceedings in the Philippines?</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Coordinated support when criminal and immigration matters intersect.</p>

    <p>Foreign nationals involved in criminal proceedings may also face separate immigration consequences, including visa, detention or deportation-related matters.</p>

    <p>Foreign Immigration Services can coordinate immigration-related assistance alongside independent Philippine legal counsel. Where legal representation is required, clients may be referred to, or assisted in coordinating with, qualified legal partners who can advise and represent them in the relevant criminal or judicial proceedings.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Assessing the immigration-related consequences of your situation</li>
      <li>Coordinating with independent Philippine legal counsel on your behalf</li>
      <li>Keeping you informed of the immigration aspects of your matter as it progresses</li>
      <li>Acting promptly where a matter is time-sensitive</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="context-note">
      <p>Foreign Immigration Services is not a law firm and does not itself provide criminal defence representation or appear in court on a client's behalf. Legal representation, where required, is provided by independent, qualified Philippine legal counsel.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="service-cta">
      <h2>Need Assistance Now?</h2>
      <p>If you or someone you know is facing a criminal or immigration proceeding in the Philippines, contact us as soon as possible.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/?service=legal-support">Request Urgent Assistance</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
